{"agent":"fleet-mergehook","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The `clean_merge_conclusion` exemption is placed *after* the scope test, so it can never fire in the default configuration, contradicting the contract the new knob advertises. With the default `[enforce].merge_commit_scope = \"own\"`, `_commit_scope` returns at the first branch (`return _merge_own_paths(tree, paths)`) and never reaches `if lease and paths and clean_merge_conclusion(tree): return []`; the exemption only exists under `\"all\"`. Concrete input: branch and `main` both edit `src/a.py` in non-overlapping regions; `git merge main` produces a clean, non-conflicted result, so `clean_merge_conclusion(tree)` is true and the commit is \"exactly git's automatic merge\". `src/a.py` is still in the staged set (the merge result differs from `HEAD`) and is part of the paths `_merge_own_paths`/the \"own\" filter keeps, so the lease check is applied to it and can refuse the merge. Running the same command with `merge_commit_scope = \"all\"` returns `[]` and allows it. That is the opposite of both claims made by the change: the knob doc says \"A merge that is exactly git's automatic merge is exempt from the lease check either way\", and `strictest=(\"all\", \"every path the merge stages is judged\")` asserts `\"all\"` is the strictest value, yet for an automatic merge it is strictly *weaker* than the default (it judges nothing on the lease check while `\"own\"` judges the same-file paths). The exemption (or the scope dispatch) needs to be ordered so the automatic-merge case is handled before the scope branch, since as written the guard is dead code for the default value.","digest":"4822604e2d5f5022","location":"ddflow/services/enforce.py:1239 (`_commit_scope`)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/enforce.py:1239 (`_commit_scope`)"}],"chunks_total":8,"coverage":"8/8 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":874280,"diff_sha":"b5d1ff914385fcf76f4cf272d0490df599418457d72fb0422e0392d724d67bf4","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":5,"files":1,"insertions":6,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":459.4,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"306948e8e54f797c","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DX-commit-hook-merge-untouched-files.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261016T023107Z-8c8aea73.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8],"reviewed_head":"7bf525e5a78d5f5395a779d0165ae6a959d5af2e","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/enforce.py:1239 (`_commit_scope`)"],"tree_sha":"7bf525e5a78d+st:a601cb38f26acd8ea29d75a696f2facb","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e47591f96205a21f841587b45","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":66056,"schema":1,"subject":"DX-commit-hook-merge-untouched-files","ts":"2026-10-16T02:38:47.592922Z"}
