{"agent":"fleet-mergehook","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`staged_diff` documents and types `paths` as the filter that \"limits it to those files\"; `None` means \"no filter\". But `paths=[]` is a distinct, valid input (it is exactly the value a caller can produce after intersecting staged paths with a branch-changed set that turned out empty), and it is not handled: the code still emits the pathspec separator, so the command becomes `git diff --cached ... --`. Git treats a bare `--` as \"everything after this is a path\" with nothing after it, i.e. no pathspec at all, so `staged_diff(repo, [])` returns the **full** staged diff rather than the empty string. That silently reintroduces the exact failure the change is fixing: a caller that filtered down to zero files (e.g. a merge whose staged content is entirely the merged parent's) would get every staged path judged instead of none. The one call site in `enforce.py` happens to be protected by the preceding `if not own: return Verdict(OK, \"\")` guard, so the bug is latent today, but the new parameter's contract is violated for `paths=[]`; the guard should be `if paths:` (falling back to `None`) or the caller must never pass an empty list. Reported because `paths: list[str] | None` explicitly admits `[]` and any future/other caller (e.g. a scope that legitimately resolves to zero paths) will get the whole diff back.","digest":"806c5b86e73e2526","location":"ddflow/services/docsync.py:staged_diff (the `*((\"--\", *paths) if paths is not None else ())` argument)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/docsync.py:staged_diff (the `*((\"--\", *paths) if paths is not None else ())` argument)"}],"chunks_total":8,"coverage":"8/8 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":874280,"diff_sha":"b5d1ff914385fcf76f4cf272d0490df599418457d72fb0422e0392d724d67bf4","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":474.8,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"e12cb278d6f8413c","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DX-commit-hook-merge-untouched-files.critic.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261016T023848Z-a1bb0a2b.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8],"reviewed_head":"7bf525e5a78d5f5395a779d0165ae6a959d5af2e","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/docsync.py:staged_diff (the `*((\"--\", *paths) if paths is not None else ())` argument)"],"tree_sha":"454737455528+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e42a3169dbfc77a546906f505","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":66077,"schema":1,"subject":"DX-commit-hook-merge-untouched-files","ts":"2026-10-16T02:46:43.397310Z"}
